<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho VII of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1157–1234</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Sancho the Strong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho VII, called the Strong, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1194 to 1234. In 1212 he fought with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and Aragon at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa</a>, a decisive Christian victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>, and the chains in Navarre's arms are said to recall it. He died childless, the last of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimenez-dynasty">Jiménez dynasty</a>, and the throne passed to his nephew Theobald of Champagne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancho-vii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Sancho VII of Navarre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Mgoni4 assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AntsoVIIArrano.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
